t 23–30 % above expected demand. Excess product 1 spoils within 5 days, and stock arriving near the top of the cycle overflows the store. Its estimated loss is similar to candidate 6's.\n5. **Candidate 3 overflows the store.** It orders every 4 days, and its large batches pile up. For example, on the morning of day 8 the stock would be about 171 against a capacity of 148, so about 23 units of product 0 are lost. This repeats in later cycles.\n6. **Candidate 4 pays the fee almost every day.** It orders on 27 days, about 1,053 in fees in total. It also has no safety stock above the forecast, so it runs short often.\n\nThe weakest calls are 1 and 5 versus 6 and 7, since 1 and 5 lead by only about 400 in my estimate. That is why their probabilities are near 0.6 rather than higher."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4642, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4642}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:45:20.312Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVSm2YMP39938uBqPiwG"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Go4PJF5uR1zqLoEcuEJZKt", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgVSm2mWTzN91LrtFtGFq", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Go4PJF5uR1zqLoEcuEJZKt", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.78, 0.62, 0.75, 0.2, 